exports[`comment > red with a recalibration proposal and the trade-off in one line 1`] = `
"<!-- twopass-eval-gate:toy -->
## ❌ Eval gate: toy
**Auto-accepted rows ≥95% right: lower bound 76.9% ❌**

Blocked by G3 promise gate:
- **promise**: auto-accepted rows ≥95.0% right: lower bound 76.9% (36/40 right)
- **confident-wrong**: auto-accepted but wrong: 0 → 4 (+4; allowance +0)

What the other gates would say: G1 aggregate threshold ✅ · G2 aggregate paired delta ✅

⚠️ No noise file: limits assume unchanged main never moves. Run \`twopass gate noise\` on unchanged main.

### Guardrails (block)

| | base | head | limit | |
|---|---:|---:|---|:-:|
| Auto-accepted rows right (Wilson lower bound) | 98.1% | 76.9% | ≥ 95% | ❌ |
| Labels losing rows beyond noise | | none | per label, min 2 | ✅ |
| Auto-accepted but wrong | 0 | 4 | +0 | ❌ |

### North Stars (reported, never block)

| | base | head |
|---|---:|---:|
| Auto-accepted | 98.0% | 20.0% |
| Sent to a person | 2.0% | 80.0% |
| Accuracy, all rows | 98.0% | 98.0% |
| Auto-accepted rows right | 100.0% | 90.0% |
| Cost per 1,000 rows (list price) | $1.00 | $1.00 |

### Recalibration proposal

**The promise holds again on held-out calibration rows; auto-accept goes from 100% to 100%.**

| on 40 held-out calibration rows | current (t0 0.5, t1 0.5, t2 0.5) | proposed (t0 0.7857, t1 0.7712, t2 0.9304) |
|---|---:|---:|
| Auto-accepted | 100.0% (40) | 100.0% (40) |
| Auto-accepted rows right | 82.5% | 100.0% |
| Wilson 95% lower bound | 68.1% | 91.2% |

Fitted on 160 calibration rows for chk at 95%; never on this PR's rows. The lower bound on 40 rows is wide; the point estimate is what the fit targets.

To apply it, commit the new thresholds (that commit goes through this gate too):

\`twopass gate recalibrate --task gates/toy.task.yaml --run head.json --write\`

<details><summary><b>Rows to read (4)</b>: changed between base and head, the riskiest auto-accepted first</summary>

| # | text | base | head | head status | confidence |
|---:|---|---|---|---|---:|
| 1 | text of alpha-000 | zzz | zzz | accepted (new) | 0.91 |
| 2 | text of beta-000 | zzz | zzz | accepted (new) | 0.91 |
| 3 | text of delta-000 | zzz | zzz | accepted (new) | 0.91 |
| 4 | text of gamma-000 | zzz | zzz | accepted (new) | 0.91 |

Gold labels are not shown: these are the rows worth a human look.
</details>

<details><summary>This run: cost, time, routing</summary>

- Rows: 200 paired. Answer flips: 0 (right→wrong 0, wrong→right 0).
- Cost (list price): base $0.200 [], head $0.200 []. Runtime: 1s + 1s.
- Thresholds: base t0 0.9 / t1 0.9 / t2 0.9; head t0 0.9 / t1 0.9 / t2 0.9.
- Routing: \`same\`
- Served: \`chk\`
- Refs: base \`base\`, head \`head\` (abcdef1)
</details>
"
`;

